    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#NodeShape"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mutex is a mechanism that enforces limits on access to a resource when there are many threads of execution. A mutex is designed to enforce a mutual exclusion concurrency control policy, and with a variety of possible methods there exists multiple unique implementations for different applications. [based on https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lock_(computer_science)]</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://ontology.unifiedcyberontology.org/uco/observable/ObservableObject"/>
  </rdf:Description>
